course: dictionary
lesson: 15892
title: Universally
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Universally is an adverb. It tells you how far something reaches: by everyone, everywhere, with no exceptions. «Kindness is universally admired.» That means people in every country admire kindness, and nobody is left out.
explain: Look for the root word inside it: universal, which means for everyone or everywhere. Adding -ly turns it into an adverb that describes how something happens. To check a meaning, swap in "by everyone, everywhere". If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Universally has a second meaning, used in science and maths. A universally true rule works in every case, not just in some. «The rule that objects fall when dropped is universally true» means it never has exceptions, so it works every time.
fact: Universally means by everyone or everywhere, without exception.
fact: Universally also means true or used in all cases.
fact: Universally is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens or how far it reaches.
fact: Common phrases: universally accepted, universally known, universally loved.
fact: Universal is the adjective, and universally is its adverb form.
exercise: «Kindness is universally admired.» What does universally mean here? | Only by a few people | *By everyone, everywhere | For one day only | In a loud voice
exercise: Maya says universally means the same as sometimes. Is she right? | Yes, because both are long words | No, universally means quietly | Yes, they mean the same thing | *No, universally means without exception, but sometimes means only now and then
exercise: «The rule that objects fall when dropped is universally true.» What does universally true mean for a rule? | It is only true on Tuesdays | *It works in every case | It was written by a scientist | It is a long, complicated rule
test: «The song is universally known in our school.» What does universally show? | *Known by everyone, with no exceptions | Known only in the music room | Known by almost nobody | Known in Spain only
test: Which phrase means accepted by everyone? | Softly spoken | *Universally accepted | Rarely seen | Quietly ignored
exam: «Respect for others is universally valued, in every country on Earth.» Which is the best swap for universally? | *By everyone, everywhere | Only at night | Quietly | Sometimes
